with no startup cost, the best bucket is 1 layer(s) on both cards —
which reproduces the lesson's H100 claim but not its B200 one.

adding a fixed per-transfer startup cost, B200's optimum moves off 1 layer at
alpha = 29.0 ms, landing on 2 layer(s) — the lesson's stated B200 answer.
So the lesson's claim holds in this model for alpha >= 29.0 ms.
The lesson does not publish alpha, so this is the model reporting what it would
take to agree, rather than a startup cost reverse-fitted to force agreement.

communication as a fraction of compute (§5's test, unhidden):
  H100: 34%   (lesson: 34%)
  B200: 77%   (lesson: 77%)

